## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical understanding of applying beginner-friendly performance optimizations and verifying them with a CI workflow in a realistic page.

## Key Concepts
- Code-splitting with dynamic imports
- Visibility-driven loading (IntersectionObserver)
- Lazy-loading media and web fonts
- Skeleton placeholders and Lighthouse budget testing
- Lighthouse CI integration

## Code Example
```javascript
import React, { Suspense, useState, useEffect } from 'react';
const HeavyWidget = React.lazy(() => import('./HeavyWidget'));

function VisibleGate({ children }) {
  const [show, setShow] = useState(false);
  useEffect(() => {
    const io = new IntersectionObserver(([e]) => {
      if (e.isIntersecting) { setShow(true); io.disconnect(); }
    });
    const el = document.getElementById('gate');
    if (el) io.observe(el);
    return () => io.disconnect();
  }, []);
  return show ? <Suspense fallback={<div className="skeleton" />}>{children}</Suspense> : null;
}

export default function Page() {
  return (
    <div>
      <div id="gate"></div>
      <VisibleGate>
        <HeavyWidget />
      </VisibleGate>
    </div>
  );
}
```

